national_interest_test_statement:
Deepening understanding of current trends in halal industries will contribute to Australia’s economic, commercial, social and cultural interests. Australia is a major player in the global halal economy as evidenced by: 

a) The Global Islamic Economy index ranked Australia the fourth-largest halal food industry in 2019; 
b) Indonesia and Malaysia are major trade partners for Australia. In 2019, Indonesia was Australia’s largest trade partner, especially for halal meat and live animals; 
c) Domestically, Australia has witnessed the growth of the domestic halal market due to an increase in its Muslim population. The 2016 census recorded that Muslims constituted 2.6% of the total Australian population, an increase of over 15% from the previous census.

The proposed research will benefit stakeholders seeking to understand the interplay between the expansion of halal goods in Australia and the region. It will contribute to educating the public, overcoming divisiveness relating to misconceptions of halal industries, building mutual understandings and social cohesiveness between Muslim minorities and the majority.
